.\"
.\" THR_JOIN(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH THR_JOIN 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
thr_join \- wait for thread termination
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/thr.h>
.PP
.BI "int thr_join(long " tid ", void **" status ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR thr_join ()
suspends execution of the calling thread until the thread specified by
.I tid
terminates.
.PP
If
.I status
is not NULL, the exit status of the terminated thread is stored in
the location pointed to by
.IR status .
.PP
The target thread must be in the same process as the caller.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned.
.PP
On error, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ESRCH
No thread with the given
.I tid
could be found in the current process.
.TP
.B EINVAL
The specified thread is not joinable.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 457
Arguments:      tid, status (on stack)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thr_new (2),
.BR thr_exit (2),
.BR pthread_join (3)
.SH HISTORY
Based on FreeBSD's thr_join(2) for BSD compatibility.
